    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profile of **Christian Yelich**, who paces our roster with a 73.63 score against Singer. His elite platoon advantage (+13%) against the right-hander makes him our premier start, while **Trea Turner** follows closely behind at 69.53. **Trea Turner** benefits from a rare combination of an elite BvP history (51 PA) and an optimized #2 spot in the order, effectively neutralizing the threat of a decent Mahle start. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** remains a locked-in core play; despite a slight park penalty, his strong dynamic platoon profile and premium spot in the order keep him well within the \"Strong\" start tier at 66.33.\n\nAggressive baserunning remains our primary strategic lever, and we are leaning into **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.79) despite a daunting matchup against Skenes. His 10% bonus for leading off and his dynamic platoon splits compensate for the SP's elite skill, though his stolen base efficiency is tempered by the 1.89s catcher pop-time risk. On the fringes, **Chase Meidroth** represents our most difficult omission; he fell just short of our 40.0 floor with a 39.88, as a negative park factor and minor platoon friction against Leahy ultimately signaled a benching to preserve our limited game caps for more favorable conditions.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile nature of the evening matchups. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (40.50) is starting, he is currently our most vulnerable asset due to an 19% SP skill penalty and an unfavorable right-on-right matchup against Miles. Should the weather or late-inning defensive substitutions shift, we are prepared to pivot to our bench reserves, though we remain largely insulated by the depth of our starters like **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16), whose top-of-the-order role against Rocker provides a stabilizing floor for our daily offensive output.",
